63
00:03:10,540 --> 00:03:12,920
In the morning, I almost
didn’t listen to it.

64
00:03:13,440 --> 00:03:15,280
Seven hours of a quiet apartment didn’t

65
00:03:15,280 --> 00:03:17,660
seem worth the time.
But on my lunch break,

66
00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:19,960
I opened it and scrolled through the audio

67
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:22,500
waveform, looking for
anything that wasn’t a

68
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:24,940
flat line. Most of it was just the hum of

69
00:03:24,940 --> 00:03:29,700
the refrigerator and the radiator ticking.
Then, at three-eleven in the morning, the

70
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:36,640
line started to move. I put my
earbuds in and pressed play. At first,

71
00:03:36,880 --> 00:03:40,080
it was just a creak, the
long, low creak an old

72
00:03:40,080 --> 00:03:41,820
